    } * std::mem::size_of::<usize>() as u64
}
```
This function first calculates the size of the current process before running the compiler and then measures the time before compilation starts. Afterwards, it creates a new instance of `LoggingHook` which is then passed to `rustc_driver::catch_with_exit_code()`. The `LazyCompileCallbacks` trait is implemented for `LoggingHook` where it sets up the logging hook and writes the session info to a log file specified in the struct. 

Once compilation finishes, the time elapsed during compilation is calculated and the size of the process after compilation is compared with that before compilation. If there was an error during compilation, the exit code will be non-zero, otherwise it will be zero.
