To update the product, you can create a form instance with an existing product and save it like so:

```python
def update_product(request, id):
    product = get_object_or_404(Product, pk=id)

    if request.method == 'POST':
        form = ProductForm(request.POST, instance=product)

        if form.is_valid():
            form.save()
            # Do something else...
    else:
        form = ProductForm(instance=product)

    return render(request, 'update_product.html', {'form': form})
```
For creating a new product, you can do the same but without passing an instance to the form constructor:

```python
